## 8. Near-miss kinds

{{table:kinds}}

The generator has five kinds:
- numeric: within one near-miss window of the threshold, on the default side;
- boundary: exactly at a strict threshold;
- subject;
- negation;
- time.

## 9. Semantics actually implemented

Measured on all test and development cases ({{semantics.all_test_and_dev.cases}} cases) and the
library ({{library_semantics.criteria}} criteria).

**Several mentions.**
- A finding criterion holds if any mention it counts has status present.
- A measurement criterion counts exactly one value, the patient's current value.
  `Criterion.evaluate` raises an error on zero or two counted values, so such states are never
  generated: {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.numeric_inputs_one_counted_value}} of
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.numeric_inputs}} measured inputs have exactly one.
- Earlier values are separate mentions with time past, and the criterion does not count them
  ({{semantics.all_test_and_dev.numeric_inputs_with_older_value}} inputs carry one).
- No measurement criterion counts past values
  ({{library_semantics.numeric_criteria_counting_past}} of {{library_semantics.numeric_criteria}}).
- There is no rule that selects the most recent of several values.

**Conflicting values.** None is generated.
- A case holds at most one mention of each finding concept:
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_inputs_two_or_more_mentions}} of
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_inputs}} finding inputs have two or more.
- A measured input has one current value; an older value is dated or marked as replaced.
- A generic absence line that could deny another present concept is left out.

**Units.**
- One unit per measured input across all templates: {{library_semantics.numeric_concepts_one_unit}}
  of {{library_semantics.numeric_concepts}} inputs have one, and
  {{library_semantics.numeric_concepts_dimensionless}} have none.
- The unit is stated in the rule text for {{library_semantics.numeric_criteria_unit_in_rule_text}}
  of the {{library_semantics.numeric_criteria_with_a_unit}} criteria with a unit.
- No edit changes a unit, and no rule needs a conversion.
- Units: {{library_semantics.units}}.

**Threshold inclusivity.**
- Operators: {{library_semantics.numeric_criteria_by_operator}}. They are stated as
  "above"/"below" (strict) and "or more"/"or less" (inclusive) and checked by
  `tests/test_library.py`.
- A value exactly at a strict threshold is the boundary near-miss.
- At an inclusive threshold the same value is a flip:
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.numeric_flips_at_threshold}} of the
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.numeric_flips_inclusive}} numeric flips at inclusive thresholds lie
  exactly on it.

**Reference date.** None.
- No case states the date of the visit
  ({{semantics.all_test_and_dev.cases_stating_a_reference_date}} cases do).
- A mention is current or past. {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.past_mentions_with_year}} of
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.past_mentions}} past mentions carry a year, from
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.dated_years_min}} to {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.dated_years_max}}.
  That is at least two years before the generator's internal year
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.generator_reference_year}}, which is not shown.
- The other past mentions say "years ago", "previously", or (superseded tier) "measured yesterday
  ... replaced".

**Window boundaries.** None.
- No criterion has a time window.
- The only rule text that names one is {{library_semantics.rule_texts_with_time_window}}: "one fall
  in the six months before this admission".
- Its program counts current falls only, and its past falls are dated two or more years back. Its
  label therefore relies on the unstated year.
- This affects {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.groups_rule_text_names_a_window}} test and development
  groups. In {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.groups_rule_text_names_a_window_time_near_miss}} of them
  the near-miss is a past fall.

**Omitted information.**
- An unmentioned history item is absent; an unmentioned measurement is unknown (`engine.ledger`).
- Labelled cases always state every measured input.
- Missing twins replace a finding line with an "unknown" line, or drop a measurement line.
- In finding bases the target concept is never named
  ({{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_bases_naming_concept}} of
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_bases}}).
  - {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_bases_generic_absence_line}} carry a generic absence line
    that does not name it.
  - {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_bases_no_line}} say nothing.
- Context findings are unmentioned in {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_inputs_unmentioned}} of
  {{semantics.all_test_and_dev.finding_inputs}} finding inputs.

## 10. Who reviewed the 450 groups, and what they checked

**People: {{reviewers.people}}.** Before the freeze, {{reviewers.sessions}} LLM agent sessions read
{{reviewers.groups}} rendered groups in two rounds:
- round 1: {{reviewers.groups_round1}} groups, 75 per session;
- round 2: {{reviewers.groups_round2}} fresh groups, after the round-1 fixes.

Each session had general tool access, read only its own sample, and edited no file. All six were
instances of the same model, which also assisted in writing the generator, so they are not
independent of it.

{{table:reviewers}}

What each session checked:
1. **Label:** does each stated answer (*s*, *s'*, or neither for a missing twin) follow from a
   literal reading of the rule and the case text?
2. **Consistency:** lines against each other, against the setting and header, and plausibility.
3. **Rendering:** grammar, units, decimals, broken text.
4. **Give-aways:** any line or wording that reveals the answer.
5. **Missing twins:** is the decisive input really unknown?

The instructions, the full reports and the rendered samples are in `audit/model_review/`.

What they found:
- **Round 1.** The sessions flagged groups whose stated answer a literal reader could dispute:
  {{review_summary.label_disputed_round1}} per session.
  - Most were missing twins whose "not recorded / not documented" wording reads as "absent".
  - Outside missing twins: {{review_summary.outside_missing_items}}.
  - No stored label disagreed with the program.
  - Fixes before the freeze:
    - "unknown" wording for missing inputs;
    - condition labels that name the counted subjects;
    - no "on arrival" in current-value templates;
    - presentation edits that keep every fact;
    - absence lines that never name the concept by a synonym;
    - setting exclusions;
    - near-misses that differ from the flip in one attribute only.
- **Round 2.** Disputed answers: {{review_summary.label_disputed_round2}} per session.
  - Consistency and rendering findings were fixed before the freeze: drawn values clashing with the
    setting, alternatives contraindicated by the condition, and the diastolic rendering.
- `docs/DECISIONS_A.md` lists every fix (rows "Pre-freeze audit 1" and "Audit round 2").

**What this does not show.**
- The reviewed groups were rendered by pre-freeze versions of the generator. No group of the frozen
  sets has been read by a person.
- The authors' reading (H1) is the first human check of text fidelity:
  - {{sample_sheets.groups}} groups ({{sample_sheets.per_set}});
  - near-miss kinds {{sample_sheets.per_kind}};
  - with {{sample_sheets.with_missing_twin}} missing twins;
  - rows per author {{sample_sheets.rows_per_author}};
  - in `audit/fidelity_author{1..4}.csv` and `audit/fidelity_sheets.md`.

## 11. Known issues

`data/rule_v1/KNOWN_ISSUES.json` lists every violation found by the re-executed checks; there are
{{target_claim_check.violations}}. The following are semantic limits, not violations, and the paper
must state them (see `docs/PAPER_VS_CODE.md`):
1. The cases have no reference date. The only rule text with a window relies on the unstated year
   (section 9).
2. A presentation edit reorders lines and rewords measured values. It never changes a unit or a
   finding's wording.
3. "At the threshold" is a near-miss kind only for strict thresholds.
4. L3-alt tests only measured criteria.
5. Base states recur between training and the sets that share its rules (L0, dev, L3-alt).
